Carafe: with d3d9.unchangedStateFastPath, a state set to the value it already has returns before the device lock.
Games that apply D3DX effects send every state of a pass on every draw, most of them unchanged. DXVK dropped those
only after taking the device lock and a stack frame: 51 ARM64 instructions per call under FEX on the A57. With the
option, SetRenderState, SetTextureStageState, SetSamplerState and SetTexture compare first and return, 25
instructions for SetRenderState; a multithreaded device or a recording state block still takes the full path.
On by default; d3d9.unchangedStateFastPath = False turns it off.
Zlib, as the files it changes.

